  "body": "If I want to define step 6.1 of https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-node-insert as mutating an underlying list (children of a node is already stated to be a list as well) I need to be able to insert.\r\n\r\nIs that acceptable? Or is that problematic for some reason?\r\n\r\nHaving this will help fix https://github.com/whatwg/dom/issues/174. The alternative I can think of is that I replace the entire list with a new list and just move the items across. Since nothing actually holds a pointer to the actual list (other than data structures DOM controls) that could probably work as well, but would be rather elaborate.",
